                <pb facs="0429" n="285" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg285"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/216: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-18T16:00:00+08:00">August 18, 1929—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 19—1:25 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>730. Legation’s 729, August 18, 2 p.m. Following from American Consul at Harbin:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“August 17, 2 p.m. Reliable reports received to the effect that clashes
                            have occurred with few casualties both sides between small detachments
                            Chinese-Soviet troops near Manchuria Station and Suifenho. Heavy
                            aircraft, Soviet artillery shooting taking place near both places
                            evidently to intimidate Chinese.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
